Ladybird now clamps the result of each filter function before the next
one applies to it. Blink does the same: RenderSurfaceFilters::
BuildImageFilter() makes each function a matrix filter of its own, with
ColorFilter::MakeMatrix(), which clamps. Chrome 158, Firefox 151 and
WebKit 26.5 (engine-compare) all give the colors Ladybird now does,
within two levels per channel, for the issue’s two filters and for
contrast(4) contrast(0.5), saturate(5) grayscale(1), hue-rotate(90deg)
invert(1), saturate(8) brightness(0.5), and a chain with a drop-shadow
between two brightness() functions.
